cientes ex possibilitate ad necessitatem productionis ducuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT6","text":"Senectus universi ex lege generali compositorum et indiciis terrestribus infertur; transitus ab defectu locali ad ruinam cosmicam breviter munitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT7","text":"Immortalitas deorum cum dissolutione compositorum hoc libro non mechanice conciliatur, quia dei causaliter semoti potius quam atomice restituti sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0067","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT8","text":"Probationes de magnitudine principiorum, infinitate spatii aliisque fundamentis prioribus libris pendent, iarumque nonnullae commissurae lacunis textus comprimuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT9","text":"Structura interne cohaeret quatenus immutabilitatem principiorum a mutabilitate ordinum constanter distinguit; maxima tensio inter leges certas naturae et clinamen incertum manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0068","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT10","text":"Restitutio verum motum textus servat: ab effectu ethico ad causam physicam, ab ea ad structuram ontologicam, deinde ad consequentiam cosmologicam et therapeuticam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T231035134041Z_9ef4f30f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Book Two","source_sha256":"657706ad03b9e80cb7d124947e76eb00b9b9666713ce1222ed3bf6877d0292fe","sha256":"cfcf9ccefaadb83abffd259b43e51ec78010ec465c36aca13ad91f4dae28000c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T23:10:35.135458+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:AS1","text":"The text asks how the motions, differences, and assemblages of principles produce qualities, living beings, worlds, and worldly changes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:AS2","text":"The nature of things consists of eternal primary bodies moving in infinite void, whose shapes, orders, positions, collisions, and motions produce all compounds without divine governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:AS3","text":"The argument is simultaneously reconstructive, diagnostic, anti-teleological, and therapeutic: it restores hidden causes from visible effects and employs knowledge of them against fear.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:AS4","text":"The movement proceeds from the insufficiency of external goods to the mechanics of principles, thence to forms and mixtures, then to the emergence of sensation, the plurality of worlds, and the mortality of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:AS5","text":"The demonstration alternates between deduced necessity, analogy from visible things, exclusion of rival models, and reduction of qualities to material arrangements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:AS6","text":"The strategic aim is to free nature from providence and closed fate, so that religious fear, fear of death, and false valuation of goods may be dissolved by natural reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A1","text":"The totality of things consists of primary bodies and infinite void.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A2","text":"Primary bodies are solid, simple, finite in magnitude, eternal, and immutable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A3","text":"The total quantity of matter neither increases nor perishes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A4","text":"Primary bodies never rest in the void.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A5","text":"Weight, blows, and the slightest clinamen constitute the causes of the motions of principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A6","text":"Bodies in a vacuum, although unequal in weight, are borne at equal speed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A7","text":"The clinamen, uncertain in place and time, breaks the necessary sequence of causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A8","text":"The shapes of principles are finite in number, but the principles of each shape are infinite in number.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A9","text":"The properties of compounds depend on the shapes, orders, positions, collisions, and motions of principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A10","text":"Every visible thing consists of several kinds of principles intermixed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A11","text":"Not all principles can be connected to one another in every way.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A12","text":"Principles lack color, smell, taste, heat, cold, sound, and sensation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A13","text":"Life and sensation arise from a fitting assemblage of insentient principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A14","text":"Death dissolves the aggregate of principles, not the principles themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A15","text":"The bodies of matter are distributed in infinite number through infinite space.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A16","text":"Gods, remote from human affairs in peace, neither create nor govern the nature of the world for the sake of human beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A17","text":"Worldly things grow while the intake of matter exceeds loss, remain steady while they are equal, and decline while loss exceeds intake.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:A18","text":"Fear of mind is dispelled by the reason of nature, not by riches, nobility, power, or sensible light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX1","text":"The pleasure of observing another's labor arises not from another's distress, but from awareness of one's own immunity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX2","text":"The nature of the body does not require gold, purple, the splendor of buildings, or great wealth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX3","text":"Riches, nobility, glory, and military force do not banish cares, religion, and fear of death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX4","text":"The darkness of the mind is not dissolved by the rays of the sun or daylight.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX5","text":"The principles of things cannot produce new motions by ceasing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX6","text":"The upward motion of flames is not spontaneous motion against weight, but the effect of an underlying force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX7","text":"Heavier bodies do not overtake lighter ones in a vacuum, nor thus produce generative blows.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX8","text":"The clinamen is not a sensible oblique motion, but the slightest deviation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX9","text":"The world was not divinely created for the sake of human beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX10","text":"The earth is properly neither a sentient goddess nor a divine mother; the mythical appellation is granted only if true causality is retained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX11","text":"The rest of visible things does not prove the rest of principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX12","text":"All principles cannot indiscriminately be connected to all things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX13","text":"The colors of things do not arise from colored principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX14","text":"The sensation of living beings is not composed from principles already sentient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX15","text":"This world is neither unique nor endowed with singular privilege as a cosmic model.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:NX16","text":"Decline in fertility and toil with advancing age are not explained by moral corruption alone or by a diminution of piety.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:D1","text":"Generation is the accession and ordering of principles, whereas destruction is their departure and redistribution.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:D2","text":"Equal falling through the void would not produce encounters unless blows and the slightest clinamen interrupted the parallelism of motions.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A4","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A5","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A6","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:D3","text":"The clinamen provides the principle of motion not fatally predetermined, whereby the will of living beings is situated within material nature.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A7","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:D4","text":"Hardness, fluidity, penetrability, and tactile effects arise from the shapes of atoms and modes of connection.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A8","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:D5","text":"Color can change without a change of principles, because it results from order, position, motion, and light.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:D6","text":"Sensation, pain, and pleasure are effects of vital motions in the compound, not affections of individual principles.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A12","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:D7","text":"The infinity of similar principles sustains the reproduction of kinds, while their laws of connection preserve distinctions.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A8","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:D8","text":"In infinite space, the same material force must produce other encounters similar to our world and other worlds.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A1","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A4","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A8","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:D9","text":"Natural order consists of the motions and limits of matter and requires no divine ruler.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A4","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:D10","text":"The world, because it is a material compound, is subject to generation, growth, maturity, and ruin.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A14","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:D11","text":"The motion of principles placed below the threshold of the senses can produce an appearance of rest in the visible totality.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A4","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:D12","text":"Knowledge of material causes weakens fearful religion and the false valuation of external goods.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A16","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:SD1","text":"The ontology of compounds is relational: the property of a thing resides not in a singular seed, but in the mode of composition.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A12","CH_0T6T_LIBS:D4","CH_0T6T_LIBS:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:SD2","text":"The system distinguishes several orders of time: immutable principles, the everlasting totality of matter, temporary assemblages, and mortal worlds.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A2","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A14","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:SD3","text":"Nature is governed neither by a fate perfectly closed nor by a will situated outside nature; the necessity of connections and indeterminate clinamen operate together.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A7","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBS:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:SD4","text":"Our world is a local assemblage within the infinite totality, not the boundary or center of things.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A1","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBS:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:SD5","text":"Life and death at the level of matter are not absolute powers, but alternations of composition and dispersion.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A13","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A14","CH_0T6T_LIBS:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:SD6","text":"The regularity of kinds arises from the selective compatibility of principles, not from a divine model or homogeneous matter.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A8","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBS:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBS:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:SD7","text":"Therapy of the mind depends on cosmology, because security is achieved by changing the map of causality, not by increasing external power.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBS:A18","CH_0T6T_LIBS:D9","CH_0T6T_LIBS:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:DNX1","text":"It must be false that visible qualities immediately manifest the intrinsic essence of principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:DNX2","text":"It must be false that every motion is necessarily connected to a new motion in a preceding order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:DNX3","text":"It must be false that the order of things presupposes a plan, human use, or a divine governor.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:DNX4","text":"It must be false that the singularity of the world or of the human being is inferred from nature itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:DNX5","text":"It must be false that the totality of things has an external boundary, bottom, or receptacle outside itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:DNX6","text":"It must be false that the identity of a thing is constituted by uniform matter; identity depends on ordered and selective mixture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:DNX7","text":"It must be false that a sensible effect can be produced only from causes of the same quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:DNX8","text":"It must be false that natural change or cosmic aging is reduced to the moral history of human beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:DNX9","text":"It must be false that rest, color, sensation, or stability observed at the visible level belong to principles in the same way.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:SNX1","text":"The totality of things is ordered around the absence of every exterior: there is nothing outside that increases or diminishes matter or redirects the universal course.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:SNX2","text":"Absolute creation and absolute annihilation are excluded; novelty arises only from a new assemblage of immutable things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:SNX3","text":"Nature lacks a center, an end of providence, and a privileged recipient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:SNX4","text":"The foundation of things is constituted through privations: principles are stable insofar as they lack mortal qualities, sensation, and change.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:SNX5","text":"No final state of generation or destruction is admitted; neither force perpetually wins the struggle of principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:SNX6","text":"The particular origin of will remains causally unavailable: the clinamen opens the fated sequence, but does not complete the transition from atomic indeterminacy to choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:FGS1","text":"Minimal natural need → false amplification of desires → impotence of external goods against fear → necessity of the reason of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:FGS2","text":"Visible effect → analogical trace → hidden material cause → exclusion of divine cause or intrinsic quality → confirmation through consequences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:FGS3","text":"Eternal bodies + infinite void → perpetual motion through weight, blows, and clinamen → assemblages and disintegrations → generation and destruction of compounds → unchanged total quantity of matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:FGS4","text":"Finite shapes × infinite instances → selective compatibility → diverse orders and positions → stable kinds and diverse properties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:FGS5","text":"Principles deprived of qualities and sensation → vital ordering → emergent sensation and qualities → disturbance of order → pain, death, and dispersion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:FGS6","text":"Infinite space + infinite matter + the same causality → multiplied encounters → innumerable worlds → removal of cosmic privilege and providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:FGS7","text":"Intake greater than loss → growth → equality → maturity → loss greater than intake → old age and ruin of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:FGS8","text":"Material map of causality → removal of religious and fatal terror → diminution of false desires → security of mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:AF1","text":"Security through doctrine → diagnosis of fear and desire → motion of principles → clinamen and will → shapes and mixtures → emergent qualities and sensation → plurality of worlds → aging of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:AF2","text":"Changeable appearance → immutable principle → material arrangement → law of connection → compound effect → exclusion of providence → cosmological and therapeutic application.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:ME1","text":"External goods are reclassified from remedies of the mind into aids limited to the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:ME2","text":"Sensible qualities are converted from primary properties of matter into effects of arrangement and relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:ME3","text":"Visible rest and stability are redescribed as effects of distance and degree of perception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:ME4","text":"Birth and death are transferred from creation and annihilation to composition and dispersion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:ME5","text":"Freedom is relocated from supernatural exemption into a natural interruption of the fated sequence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:ME6","text":"The difference of species and the constancy of kinds are explained by laws of material compatibility, not by exemplary forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:ME7","text":"The world is reclassified from a unique creation into a local, replicable, and mortal assemblage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:ME8","text":"Gods are transferred from causal rulers into remote and causally idle natures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:ME9","text":"The decline of the earth is changed from a sign of moral corruption into a phase of the world's material cycle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:ALT1","text":"The surface level comprises human fears, desires, sensible qualities, visible motions, and signs of growth and old age.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:ALT2","text":"The structural level comprises primary bodies, void, weight, blows, clinamen, shapes, mixtures, and laws of connection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level converts appearances into traces of causes and reconstitutes the contest between providence, fate, and material naturalism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level distinguishes immutable principles, mortal compositions, the everlasting totality, and plural worlds subject to generation and ruin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT1","text":"The proposed axioms suffice to reconstruct the sequence from the mechanics of principles to emergence, cosmology, and therapy of the mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT2","text":"The firmest part of the system is the conjunction of the conservation of matter with a configurational explanation of generation, qualities, and death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT3","text":"The connection between the slightest clinamen and conscious will is not mechanically demonstrated, but inferred from the necessity of breaking fate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT4","text":"Explanations of qualities from shapes and motions often rely on sensible analogy and do not determine an exact correspondence between shape and effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT5","text":"The deduction of innumerable worlds employs a principle of plenitude: sufficient matter, place, and cause lead from possibility to the necessity of production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT6","text":"The aging of the universe is inferred from the general law of compounds and terrestrial indications; the transition from local decline to cosmic ruin is briefly supported.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT7","text":"The immortality of the gods is not mechanically reconciled in this book with the dissolution of compounds, because the gods are reconstructed as causally remote rather than atomically.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0044","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0067","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT8","text":"Demonstrations concerning the magnitude of principles, the infinity of space, and other foundations depend on earlier books, and some of their joints are compressed by gaps in the text.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT9","text":"The structure coheres internally insofar as it consistently distinguishes the immutability of principles from the mutability of orders; the greatest tension remains between the fixed laws of nature and uncertain clinamen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0068","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBS:MRT10","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text: from ethical effect to physical cause, from this to ontological structure, then to cosmological and therapeutic consequence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBS:PRB1C6EDC6412FDF59:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_0T6T_LIBS@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_0T6T_LIBS:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 02","title":"Book Two","context":"Chapter 02","original_title":"Liber Secundus","original_context":"Chapter 02"},"original_title":"Liber Secundus","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT","layer":"CH","title":"Book Three","order":3,"parents":["RAW_0T6T_LIBT"],"revision":"CH_0T6T_LIBT@R001","sha256":"22dc21a311f228f2bd0efbb2eab5e4863a5d1aced5b4bcc2781e36fa6272cfc0","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AS1","text":"Quaeritur quomodo cognitio naturae animi et animae metum mortis, radicem perturbationis humanae, auferre possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AS2","text":"Thesis principalis est naturam animi animaeque corpoream, coniunctam, nativam ac mortalem esse, unde mors ad eum qui iam non est nihil pertineat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AS3","text":"Argumentatio diagnostica, physice reconstructiva, polemica et therapeutica est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AS4","text":"Doctrina primordiorum et inanis fundamentum praebet quo terrores divini, Acheruntis opiniones et immortalitas animae dissolvantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AS5","text":"Motus argumenti procedit ab effectibus timoris ad structuram corporis et animae, deinde a coniunctione, alteratione ac divisione ad mortalitatem, postremo a mortalitate ad nullitatem mali post mortem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AS6","text":"Conclusio physica in conversionem ethicam transit: qui causam perturbationis novit nec mortem fugit nec vitam indefinita possessione, potentia aut mutatione loci explere conatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A1","text":"Res naturales ex primordiis corporeis motu aeterno per inane componuntur et dissolvuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A2","text":"Metus mortis et Acheruntis praecipua radix est avaritiae, ambitionis, invidiae, proditionis atque odii vitae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A3","text":"Terror animi non radiis diei, religione aut professione verbali, sed naturae specie rationeque dissolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A4","text":"Animus et anima sunt partes constitutivae hominis, non habitus corporis sine sede aut substantia propria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A5","text":"Animus et anima coniuncti unam naturam efficiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A6","text":"Animus in pectore situs consilium ac regimen tenet, anima autem per corpus dissita motibus eius consentit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A7","text":"Actio physica fit per tactum, tactus autem sine corpore esse non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A8","text":"Natura animi animaeque corporea est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A9","text":"Natura animi animaeque ex subtilissimis seminibus caloris, venti, aeris et quartae potestatis nomine carentis componitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10","text":"Sensus ex communibus corporis, animi atque animae motibus oritur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A11","text":"Animus et anima una cum corpore gignuntur, crescunt, senescunt, aegrescunt et labefactantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A12","text":"Quod mutari, dividi, dissipari aut ordine partium transferri potest aeternum esse non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A13","text":"Animus et anima certis corporis sedibus, organis et complexionibus indigent ut nascantur, permaneant et sentiant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A14","text":"Aeternum manet aut quia ictus soliditate respuit, aut quia ictibus caret, aut quia nullum locum externum habet in quem dissolvatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","text":"Persona humana ex coniunctione corporis, animi et animae atque ex continuitate motuum sensiferorum constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16","text":"Incommodum alicui accidere non potest nisi idem subiectum tempore incommodi existat et sentiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A17","text":"Vita nulli mancipio datur, sed omnibus ad tempus usu conceditur, dum materia ad formas posteriores transit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A18","text":"Poenae Acheruntis sunt figurae timoris, cupiditatis, ambitionis, insatiabilitatis et conscientiae scelerum quae in vita operantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX1","text":"Animus non est harmonia neque habitus vitalis corporis nulla in parte situs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX2","text":"Anima neque incorporea neque simplex est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX3","text":"Animus non per oculos quasi per fores separatus spectat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX4","text":"Corpus vivum non est instrumentum prorsus expers sensus, quia sentit ex coniunctione cum anima.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX5","text":"Primordia animae non singulis corporis primordiis alternatim adposita sunt, contra Democriti sententiam relatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX6","text":"Animus et anima non possunt extra corpus integre vivere, sentire aut motus vitales continuare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX7","text":"Anima non est substantia immortalis extrinsecus insinuata, ante corpus perfecta aut inter corpora transmigrans.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX8","text":"Sensus post mortem sine oculis, auribus, naribus, lingua, manibus ceterisque organis consistere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX9","text":"Acheron, Tartarus, Cerberus, Furiae et poenae infernae non sunt loca aut res post mortem existentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX10","text":"Mors non est malum quod mortuus pati, desiderare aut deplorare possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX11","text":"Lumen diei, religio intensior et professio audaciae metum occultum non tollunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX12","text":"Mutatio loci, divitiarum, honoris aut occupationis causam perturbationis interioris non removet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D1","text":"Contemptus, egestas et obscuritas, quia mortis quasi limina aestimantur, cupiditatem opum atque honorum acuunt.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D2","text":"Metus mortis, dum mortem evitare conatur, ad proditionem, caedem, dissolutionem amicitiae et mortem voluntariam impellere potest.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A2","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D3","text":"Reciproca efficacia animi et corporis, qua metus membra concutit et vulnera mentem afficiunt, coniunctionem corporalem demonstrat.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A6","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A7","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D4","text":"Quia calor, ventus et aer soli sensum explicare non possunt, quarta vis subtilior ponitur quae motum sensiferum prima initiet.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D5","text":"Quia minima externa corpus tangunt antequam sentiantur, primordia animae rarius quam primordia corporis per membra distributa sunt.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D6","text":"Communis ortus, incrementum, senectus, morbus, ebrietas et curatio animi cum corpore mortalitatem animi indicant.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D7","text":"Gradualis sensus amissio et divisio animae cum membris ostendunt animam partibilem atque ideo mortalem esse.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A8","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D8","text":"Quia sensus a certa dispositione corporis et animae pendet, anima e corpore eiecta neque contineri neque sentire potest.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D9","text":"Dissoluta coniunctione constitutiva, nullum idem subiectum superest cui mors nocere possit.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D6","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D7","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D10","text":"Etiam perfecta eiusdem materiae futura recompositio ad nos non pertineret, si continuitas vitae et memoriae semel interrupta esset.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A1","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D11","text":"Insensibilitas temporis ante ortum exemplar praebet insensibilitatis temporis post mortem.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D12","text":"Dolor de propria putrefactione aut laceratione post mortem nascitur ex tacita fictione qua vivus se corpori mortuo adhuc sentientem adstat.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D13","text":"Fabulae infernae futurum locum non describunt, sed passiones, poenas civiles et conscientiae cruciatus praesentis vitae figurant.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A2","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D14","text":"Qui causam perturbationis ignorat se ipsum per mutationem loci fugit, sed causam secum transfert.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A2","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D15","text":"Productio vitae non minuit futurum tempus non-exsistentiae, quia nullus mortuus diutius aut brevius mortem sentit.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D16","text":"Successio formarum requirit ut vetustas novitati cedat et materia post vitam ad postera saecla redeat.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A1","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD1","text":"Physica fit therapeutica, quia correcta ontologia animi tollit subiectum imaginarium cui supplicia post mortem tribuebantur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D8","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD2","text":"Mortalitas animae multipliciter firmatur per compositionem, dependentiam organicam, alterationem, divisibilitatem, localizationem et dissolutionem.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A12","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A13","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D6","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD3","text":"Etiam concessa per hypothesim aliqua sensatione animae separatae, illa ad nos non pertineret sine continuitate coniunctionis qua persona constituitur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD4","text":"Avaritia, ambitio, invidia et violentia politica denuo intelliguntur ut artes fallaces quibus homo mortem symbolicam per opes, potentiam aut nomen vitare conatur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D1","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD5","text":"Persona non est substantia simplex inter corpora migrans, sed temporaria ordinatio corporis, animi, animae et motuum sensiferorum.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A5","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD6","text":"Tempus ante ortum et tempus post mortem ontologice respondent, quamquam imaginatio posterius falso quasi experientiam futuram repraesentat.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D11","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD7","text":"Sufficientia vitae non ex indefinita duratione aut novitate rerum, sed ex termino cupiditatis et aequa cessationis acceptione oritur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A17","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD8","text":"Mythologia inferorum in cartam affectuum praesentium convertitur, qua terror divinus, libido, ambitio, insatiabilitas et culpa diversis figuris ordinantur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A18","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet dualismum secundum quem mens integra corpori extrinsecus advenit et ab eo separata easdem operationes retinet.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A7","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet subiectum propriae non-exsistentiae testem, victimam aut possessorem esse posse.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet identitatem personalem ex sola identitate materiae sine continuitate sensus et memoriae restitui.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet naturam immortalem substantialiter mutari, aegrescere, sanari, dividi aut ordinem partium commutare posse.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A12","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet infinitam vitae productionem novitatem qualitativam aut ultimam satietatem necessario parere.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse debet opes, honores, nomen aut potentiam metum mortis abolere posse.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D1","CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX7","text":"Falsum esse debet ordinem moralem post mortem per loca, iudices et tormenta externa compleri.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A18","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX8","text":"Falsum esse debet perturbationem interiorem mutatione domicilii, itineris aut occupationis curari posse.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX9","text":"Falsum esse debet professionem doctrinalem firmam convictionem probare, quia adversitas opiniones tacitas aperit.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX1","text":"Nulla res transcendens personam integram post dissolutionem corporis reservat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX2","text":"Nullus prospectus personalis trans mortis terminum continuatur ex quo mors ut status proprius experiatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX3","text":"Nulla exceptio individualis hominem a communi compositionis, dissolutionis et restitutionis materiae lege eximit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX4","text":"Nullum obiectum futurum cupiditatem per se claudit, quia desiderium absentis post adeptam rem in aliud transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX5","text":"Nullum theatrum posthumum requiritur ut culpa puniatur, quia mens sibi conscia poenam praesentem anticipando constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX6","text":"Vita neque perpetua possessio neque debitum naturae est, sed usus temporarius materiae communis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX7","text":"Mors non est experientia extrema vitae, sed terminus quo ipsa possibilitas experientiae aufertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS1","text":"Machina epistemica initium capit hac serie: primordia et inane → natura sine interventu divino explicabilis → moenia mundi aperta → terror religiosus imminutio.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A1","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS2","text":"Machina diagnostica hac serie operatur: metus mortis → egestas et contemptus quasi mortis imagines → opes, honores et violentia ut fugae → maior perturbatio.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A2","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D1","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS3","text":"Machina reconstructiva procedit per distinctionem: animus centralis et regens / anima diffusa et consentiens / corpus commune / motus sensifer ex coniunctione.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A4","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A5","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A6","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS4","text":"Machina mortalitatis hac serie concludit: compositio corporea → dependentia organica → communis alteratio → divisibilitas → dissipatio → impossibilitas immortalitatis.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A8","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A12","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS5","text":"Machina identitatis hac serie clauditur: dissolutio coniunctionis → interruptio continuitatis → absentia eiusdem subiecti → impossibilitas mali post mortem.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D9","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS6","text":"Machina temporalis utitur symmetria: nulla experientia ante ortum → nulla experientia post dissolutionem → posteritas non magis timenda quam praeterita vetustas.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D11","CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS7","text":"Machina mythologica convertit inferos futuros in figuras passionum, poenarum et conscientiae iam praesentium.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A18","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D13","CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS8","text":"Machina therapeutica concludit: cognitio causae → cessatio fugae exterioris → limitatio cupiditatis → acceptio mortalitatis → tranquillitas vitae finitae.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D14","CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AF1","text":"Epicuri ratio naturae → diagnosis timoris Acheruntis → constitutio corporea animi et animae → probatio mortalitatis → remotio subiecti post mortem → mors nihil ad nos → conversio vitae praesentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AF2","text":"Motus probatorius est: efficacia tactilis → corporeitas → compositio subtilis → coniunctio organica → alteratio et divisio → dissolutio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AF3","text":"Motus therapeuticus est: terror occultus → cupiditas compensatoria → frustratio recursiva → cognitio causae → terminus desiderii → aequa cessatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME1","text":"Mens et anima ex substantiis separabilibus in organizationem materialem localem et mortalem transferuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME2","text":"Sensus ex proprietate animae solitariae in effectum communium motuum corporis, animi et animae reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME3","text":"Mors ex statu futuro ab homine patiendo in absentiam subiecti patientis convertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME4","text":"Avaritia, ambitio, invidia et violentia ex vitiis discretis in effectus secundarios timoris mortis rediguntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME5","text":"Identitas personalis non amplius ex materia eadem, sed ex coniunctione et continuitate motuum sensiferorum describitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME6","text":"Inferi ex geographia posthuma in cartam passionum, poenarum civilium et conscientiae praesentis transferuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME7","text":"Ager therapeuticus a religione, mutatione loci et amplificatione vitae ad cognitionem naturae et limitationem cupiditatis transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei tractat metum mortis, naturam animi animaeque et quaestionem num aliquid post mortem sentiri possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis exponit compositionem atomicam, localizationem, hierarchiam animi et animae, coniunctionem organicam atque productionem sensus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus mutat certamen contra mortem in certamen contra errorem quo vivus se post mortem adhuc sentientem fingit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis personam definit ut coniunctionem materialem finitam, identitatem ut continuitatem, mortem ut interruptionem et materiam ut successionis communis fundamentum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad restituendam seriem a physica animi per probationem mortalitatis ad conclusionem mortem nihil ad nos esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT2","text":"Minus determinatus manet transitus a figuris et mobilitate primordiorum ad qualitatem sensus, quam quarta natura nomine carens explere debet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT3","text":"Lacunae fontis nexus locales circa refutationem harmoniae et condiciones immortalitatis minuunt, sed motum principalem non interrumpunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT4","text":"Systema maxime cohaeret ubi dependentiam organicam, alterationem, divisionem et absentiam subiecti in probationem cumulativam coniungit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT5","text":"Firmissima clausura est quod malum sine subiecto sentiente consistere non potest, etiam si hypothesis aliqua posthuma ad tempus concedatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT6","text":"Commissura fragilis est principium secundum quod omnis mutatio substantialis morti rei prioris aequiparatur, quia hoc principium potius assumitur quam plene demonstratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0045","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT7","text":"Tensio manet inter unitatem animi et animae atque hierarchiam qua animus dominatur, anima paret et quarta vis sensum initiare dicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0027","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT8","text":"Restitutio verum motum textus servat: indicia perturbationis → physica coniunctionis → mortalitas → nulla experientia mortis → reordinatio vitae praesentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T231124010402Z_adeb3140","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Book Three","source_sha256":"22dc21a311f228f2bd0efbb2eab5e4863a5d1aced5b4bcc2781e36fa6272cfc0","sha256":"7658da8777306e48e3180c44a26455a24b64246b8838a4fb94dea7cb0cb8ae6e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T23:11:29.324569+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AS1","text":"It is asked how knowledge of the nature of the mind and soul can remove the fear of death, the root of human disturbance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AS2","text":"The principal thesis is that the nature of the mind and soul is corporeal, conjoined, born, and mortal, whence death pertains in no way to one who no longer exists.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AS3","text":"The argumentation is diagnostic, physically reconstructive, polemical, and therapeutic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AS4","text":"The doctrine of first-beginnings and void provides the foundation by which divine terrors, beliefs about Acheron, and the immortality of the soul are dissolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AS5","text":"The movement of the argument proceeds from the effects of fear to the structure of body and soul, then from conjunction, alteration, and division to mortality, and finally from mortality to the nullity of evil after death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AS6","text":"The physical conclusion passes into an ethical conversion: one who knows the cause of disturbance neither flees death nor tries to fill life through indefinite possession, power, or change of place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A1","text":"Natural things are compounded and dissolved from corporeal first-beginnings in eternal motion through the void.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A2","text":"Fear of death and of Acheron is the chief root of greed, ambition, envy, treachery, and hatred of life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A3","text":"Terror of mind is dissolved not by the rays of day, religion, or verbal profession, but by the aspect and reason of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A4","text":"Mind and soul are constitutive parts of the human being, not a condition of the body without a seat or substance of their own.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A5","text":"Mind and soul conjoined produce one nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A6","text":"The mind, situated in the breast, holds deliberation and governance, while the soul, dispersed through the body, accords with its motions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A7","text":"Physical action occurs through touch, and touch cannot exist without body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A8","text":"The nature of mind and soul is corporeal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A9","text":"The nature of mind and soul is composed of the most subtle seeds of heat, wind, air, and a fourth power lacking a name.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10","text":"Sensation arises from the shared motions of body, mind, and soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A11","text":"Mind and soul are generated, grow old, become diseased, and are weakened together with the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A12","text":"What can be changed, divided, dissipated, or transferred by an ordering of parts cannot be eternal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A13","text":"Mind and soul require definite seats, organs, and constitutions of the body in order to be born, persist, and sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A14","text":"What is eternal remains so either because it repels blows by solidity, or because it lacks blows, or because it has no external place into which it may dissolve.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","text":"The human person is constituted from the conjunction of body, mind, and soul, and from the continuity of sentient motions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16","text":"A harm cannot happen to anyone unless that same subject exists and senses at the time of the harm.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A17","text":"Life is given to no one as property, but granted to all for temporary use, while matter passes into later forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:A18","text":"The punishments of Acheron are figures of fear, desire, ambition, insatiability, and consciousness of crimes operating in life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX1","text":"The mind is neither harmony nor a vital condition of the body situated in no part.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX2","text":"The soul is neither incorporeal nor simple.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX3","text":"The mind does not see separately through the eyes as though through doors.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX4","text":"The living body is not an instrument wholly devoid of sensation, because it senses through conjunction with the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX5","text":"The first-beginnings of the soul are not placed alternately alongside the individual first-beginnings of the body, contrary to the reported view of Democritus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX6","text":"Mind and soul cannot live, sense, or continue vital motions intact outside the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX7","text":"The soul is not an immortal substance introduced from without, complete before the body, or transmigrating among bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX8","text":"Sensation after death cannot subsist without eyes, ears, nostrils, tongue, hands, and the other organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX9","text":"Acheron, Tartarus, Cerberus, the Furies, and infernal punishments are not places or things existing after death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX10","text":"Death is not an evil that the dead person can suffer, desire, or lament.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX11","text":"The light of day, more intense religion, and a profession of boldness do not remove hidden fear.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX12","text":"A change of place, wealth, honor, or occupation does not remove the cause of inner disturbance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D1","text":"Contempt, poverty, and obscurity, because they are judged to be as it were thresholds of death, sharpen the desire for wealth and honors.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D2","text":"Fear of death, while attempting to avoid death, can impel one toward treachery, slaughter, the dissolution of friendship, and voluntary death.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A2","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D3","text":"The reciprocal efficacy of mind and body, whereby fear shakes the limbs and wounds affect the mind, demonstrates corporeal conjunction.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A6","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A7","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D4","text":"Because heat, wind, and air alone cannot explain sensation, a subtler fourth force is posited that first initiates sentient motion.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D5","text":"Because the smallest external things touch the body before they are sensed, the first-beginnings of the soul are distributed through the limbs more sparsely than the first-beginnings of the body.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D6","text":"The shared origin, growth, old age, disease, drunkenness, and treatment of mind with body indicate the mortality of mind.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D7","text":"The gradual loss of sensation and the division of the soul with the limbs show that the soul is divisible and therefore mortal.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A8","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D8","text":"Because sensation depends on a definite disposition of body and soul, the soul expelled from the body can neither be contained nor sense.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D9","text":"Once the constitutive conjunction is dissolved, no same subject remains to which death can do harm.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D6","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D7","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D10","text":"Even a future perfect recomposition of the same matter would not pertain to us if the continuity of life and memory had once been interrupted.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A1","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D11","text":"The insensibility of time before birth provides a model for the insensibility of time after death.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D12","text":"Pain concerning one's own putrefaction or mutilation after death arises from the tacit fiction by which, living, one imagines oneself still present to the dead body as sensing.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D13","text":"Infernal tales do not describe a future place, but figure the passions, civil punishments, and torments of conscience of present life.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A2","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D14","text":"One who does not know the cause of disturbance flees oneself through a change of place, but carries the cause along.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A2","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D15","text":"The prolongation of life does not diminish future time of non-existence, because no dead person senses death for longer or shorter.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:D16","text":"The succession of forms requires that oldness yield to newness and that matter return after life to later ages.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A1","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD1","text":"Physics becomes therapeutic because a corrected ontology of mind removes the imaginary subject to which punishments after death were attributed.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D8","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD2","text":"The mortality of the soul is established in multiple ways through composition, organic dependence, alteration, divisibility, localization, and dissolution.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A12","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A13","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D6","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD3","text":"Even if some sensation of the separated soul were granted by hypothesis, it would not pertain to us without the continuity of conjunction by which the person is constituted.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD4","text":"Greed, ambition, envy, and political violence are understood anew as deceptive arts by which a human being attempts to avoid symbolic death through wealth, power, or name.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D1","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD5","text":"The person is not a simple substance migrating among bodies, but a temporary ordering of body, mind, soul, and sentient motions.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A5","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD6","text":"Time before birth and time after death correspond ontologically, although imagination falsely represents the latter as though it were a future experience.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D11","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD7","text":"The sufficiency of life arises not from indefinite duration or novelty of things, but from the limit of desire and an equitable acceptance of cessation.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A17","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD8","text":"The mythology of the underworld is converted into a map of present affects, in which divine terror, desire, ambition, insatiability, and guilt are arranged under diverse figures.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A18","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX1","text":"It must be false that dualism according to which an intact mind comes to the body from without and, separated from it, retains the same operations.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A7","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX2","text":"It must be false that a subject can be witness, victim, or possessor of its own non-existence.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX3","text":"It must be false that personal identity is restored from identity of matter alone without continuity of sensation and memory.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX4","text":"It must be false that an immortal nature can be substantially changed, become diseased, be healed, divided, or alter the order of its parts.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A12","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX5","text":"It must be false that an infinite prolongation of life necessarily produces qualitative novelty or ultimate satiety.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0063","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX6","text":"It must be false that wealth, honors, name, or power can abolish the fear of death.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D1","CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX7","text":"It must be false that the moral order is fulfilled after death through places, judges, and external torments.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A18","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX8","text":"It must be false that inner disturbance can be cured by a change of dwelling, journey, or occupation.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:DNX9","text":"It must be false that doctrinal profession proves firm conviction, because adversity reveals tacit beliefs.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBT:NX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX1","text":"No transcendent thing preserves the intact person after the dissolution of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX2","text":"No personal perspective continues beyond the boundary of death from which death might be experienced as one's own state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX3","text":"No individual exception exempts a human being from the common law of composition, dissolution, and restoration of matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX4","text":"No future object closes desire by itself, because desire for what is absent transfers to another thing once the thing has been attained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX5","text":"No posthumous theater is required for guilt to be punished, because the self-conscious mind constitutes present punishment by anticipating it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX6","text":"Life is neither perpetual possession nor a debt owed to nature, but the temporary use of common matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:SNX7","text":"Death is not the ultimate experience of life, but the boundary at which the very possibility of experience is removed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS1","text":"The epistemic machine begins with this sequence: first-beginnings and void → nature explicable without divine intervention → walls of the world opened → diminution of religious terror.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A1","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS2","text":"The diagnostic machine operates through this sequence: fear of death → poverty and contempt as images of death → wealth, honors, and violence as escapes → greater disturbance.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A2","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D1","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS3","text":"The reconstructive machine proceeds through a distinction: central and governing mind / diffuse and accordant soul / common body / sentient motion from conjunction.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A4","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A5","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A6","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS4","text":"The mortality machine concludes through this sequence: corporeal composition → organic dependence → shared alteration → divisibility → dissipation → impossibility of immortality.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A8","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A12","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS5","text":"The identity machine closes through this sequence: dissolution of conjunction → interruption of continuity → absence of the same subject → impossibility of evil after death.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBT:A16","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D9","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS6","text":"The temporal machine employs symmetry: no experience before birth → no experience after dissolution → posterity no more to be feared than past antiquity.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:D11","CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS7","text":"The mythological machine converts the future underworld into figures of passions, punishments, and conscience already present.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A18","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D13","CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:FGS8","text":"The therapeutic machine concludes: knowledge of the cause → cessation of external flight → limitation of desire → acceptance of mortality → tranquility of finite life.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBT:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBT:D14","CH_0T6T_LIBT:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AF1","text":"Epicurus' account of nature → diagnosis of fear of Acheron → corporeal constitution of mind and soul → proof of mortality → removal of the subject after death → death is nothing to us → conversion of present life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AF2","text":"The probative movement is: tactile efficacy → corporeality → subtle composition → organic conjunction → alteration and division → dissolution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:AF3","text":"The therapeutic movement is: hidden terror → compensatory desire → recurrent frustration → knowledge of the cause → limit of desire → equitable cessation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME1","text":"Mind and soul are transferred from separable substances into a local and mortal material organization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME2","text":"Sensation is reclassified from a property of the solitary soul into an effect of the shared motions of body, mind, and soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME3","text":"Death is converted from a future state to be undergone by a human being into the absence of a subject undergoing it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME4","text":"Greed, ambition, envy, and violence are reduced from distinct vices to secondary effects of fear of death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME5","text":"Personal identity is no longer described from the same matter, but from conjunction and the continuity of sentient motions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME6","text":"The underworld is transferred from posthumous geography into a map of passions, civil punishments, and present conscience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ME7","text":"The therapeutic field is transferred from religion, change of place, and enlargement of life to knowledge of nature and limitation of desire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ALT1","text":"The surface level treats fear of death, the nature of mind and soul, and the question whether anything can be sensed after death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ALT2","text":"The structural level expounds atomic composition, localization, the hierarchy of mind and soul, organic conjunction, and the production of sensation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level changes the struggle against death into a struggle against the error by which the living person imagines oneself still sensing after death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level defines the person as a finite material conjunction, identity as continuity, death as interruption, and matter as the foundation of common succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the sequence from the physics of mind through proof of mortality to the conclusion that death is nothing to us.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT2","text":"Less determinate remains the transition from the shapes and mobility of first-beginnings to the quality of sensation, which the nameless fourth nature must fulfill.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT3","text":"Gaps in the source lessen local connections around the refutation of harmony and the conditions of immortality, but do not interrupt the principal movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT4","text":"The system is most coherent where it joins organic dependence, alteration, division, and absence of the subject into a cumulative proof.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT5","text":"The strongest closure is that evil cannot subsist without a sensing subject, even if some posthumous hypothesis is conceded temporarily.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT6","text":"A fragile joint is the principle according to which every substantial change is equated with the death of the prior thing, because this principle is assumed rather than fully demonstrated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0035","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0045","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT7","text":"A tension remains between the unity of mind and soul and the hierarchy by which mind rules, soul obeys, and the fourth force is said to initiate sensation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0027","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBT:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text: signs of disturbance → physics of conjunction → mortality → no experience of death → reordering of present life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBT:PR2291A2AD738E2FD6:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_0T6T_LIBT@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_0T6T_LIBT:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 03","title":"Book Three","context":"Chapter 03","original_title":"Liber Tertius","original_context":"Chapter 03"},"original_title":"Liber Tertius","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ","layer":"CH","title":"Book Four","order":4,"parents":["RAW_0T6T_LIBQ"],"revision":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ@R001","sha256":"aa8b66df6ee726125bd9404c1e7becd8fd69f15d798891c3c3dadecfa20c5ddf","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:AS1","text":"Quaeritur quomodo perceptio, cogitatio, somnus, actio, cupiditas et generatio ex principiis corporeis explicari possint sine animis immortalibus, providentia aut causis finalibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:AS2","text":"Omnes hae operationes ex emissione, transmissione, congruentia et ictu corporum tenuissimorum oriuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est materialiter reconstructiva, adversus superstitionem, scepticismum et finalitatem polemica, atque doctrinae asperae lepore poetico tradendae strategice accommodata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:AS4","text":"Ex doctrina primordiorum proceditur ad necessitatem simulacrorum, inde ad mechanismum visionis et ad apparentium errorum dissolutionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:AS5","text":"Defensio sensuum errorem ab affectione sensibili ad opiniones animi transfert atque sensus fundamentum rationis constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:AS6","text":"Eadem grammatica corporei contactus ad auditum, saporem, odorem, cogitationem, somnum, voluntatem et motum extenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:AS7","text":"Analysis denique ad usum membrorum, cupiditatem Veneream, captivitatem amoris et generationem transfertur, ut causalitas naturalis simul cognitionem et regimen affectuum ordinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A1","text":"Omnes res, animus atque anima inclusi, ex primordiis corporeis componuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A2","text":"Primordia figura, magnitudine, motu, ordine et textura differunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A3","text":"Ex rebus corpora perpetuo fluunt et in omnes partes emittuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A4","text":"Simulacra sunt texturae tenuissimae quae a superficie rerum emissae formam coloremque originis servant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A5","text":"Omnis sensus corporeo ictu proprii nuntii movetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A6","text":"Cuique sensui potestas propria et ab aliis sensibus distincta est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A7","text":"Qualitas sensibilis ex congruentia figurarum incidentium cum viis et textura recipientis oritur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A8","text":"Tenuitas, medium, spatium, obstacula et rectitudo itineris transmissionem corporum determinant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A9","text":"Simulacra possunt in aere constitui vel ex imaginibus diversarum rerum coalescere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A10","text":"Animus simulacris tenuioribus quam quae oculos movent corpore penetrantibus lacessitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A11","text":"Animus ex copia imaginum eas potissimum recipit ad quas attentione, habitu aut statu corporis praeparatus est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A12","text":"Quod cuique sensui suo tempore apparet verum est quatenus affectio illius sensus est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A13","text":"Falsitas oritur ex opinionibus quas animus rebus sensu datis adiungit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A14","text":"Notitia veri a sensibus initium capit, atque ratio sensuum fide nititur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A15","text":"Structura membrorum usum antecedit, et quod natum est facultatem utendi postea gignit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A16","text":"Vita animalis a distributione, coniunctione et motibus animae corporeae per membra pendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A17","text":"Voluntas agendi oritur postquam animus imaginem actionis futurae concepit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A18","text":"Cupiditas Venerea est perturbatio materialis seminis a simulacro vel corpore congruo excitata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A19","text":"Partus ex concursu et congruentia seminum maternorum atque paternorum constat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:NX1","text":"Simulacra mortuorum non probant animas ab Acherunte redire neque aliquid personale post corporis et animi dissolutionem superesse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:NX2","text":"Simulacra singillatim videri non possunt, quamvis creber eorum concursus rem visibilem efficiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:NX3","text":"Fallaciae perspectivae non demonstrant oculos ipsos mentiri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:NX4","text":"Sententia nihil sciri posse se ipsam sine contradictione affirmare non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:NX5","text":"Ratio a sensibus orta sensus tamquam universaliter falsos refellere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:NX6","text":"Unus sensus potestatem propriam alterius sensus iudicare aut convincere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:NX7","text":"Centauri, Scyllae et imagines mortuorum non requirunt naturas animatas sibi correspondentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:NX8","text":"Echoes et soni repercussi Satyrorum, Nympharum, Faunorum aut Panis praesentiam non requirunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:NX9","text":"Simulacra voluntatem humanam non perspiciunt neque arte instructa motus somniorum componunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:NX10","text":"Oculi, lingua, aures et membra non sunt ad futuros usus creata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:NX11","text":"Somnus non est plena animae e corpore expulsio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:NX12","text":"Sterilitas et fecunditas non a numinibus divinis distribuuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0082","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:NX13","text":"Voluptas Venerea amorem exclusivum non requirit, neque amor possessione corporis amati satiatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D1","text":"Repentina imago specularis ex adsiduo simulacrorum fluxu et repercussu oritur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A4","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D2","text":"Simulacra ob tenuitatem, levitatem et positionem superficialem figuram servant atque velocissime feruntur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A2","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A4","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D3","text":"Visio fit cum simulacrum oculos ferit, distantia autem ex aere interposito ante imaginem moto percipitur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A4","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A5","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D4","text":"Situs, inversio et multiplicatio imaginum specularium ex ordine aerum, repercussionum et flexuum superficiei oriuntur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A4","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D5","text":"Figurae remotae, lumina, umbrae et corpora refracta aliter apparent cum transmissio ictibus, intervallis aut mediis mutatur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A5","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A7","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D6","text":"Apparentia sensibilis recte praesentem affectionem indicat, dum error ex iudicio de causa, identitate aut motu rei nascitur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A12","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A13","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D7","text":"Vox corpus est quod a loquente emissum aures ferit, per spatium confunditur, in plures partes dividitur et a solidis repercutitur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A2","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A5","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D8","text":"Sapores et odores secundum figuram particularum, magnitudinem viarum et texturam animalis diversa vel contraria efficiunt.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A2","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A5","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A7","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D9","text":"Monstra imaginata ex concursu imaginum verarum partium componuntur, non ex existentia monstrorum correspondentium.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D10","text":"In somno simulacra mentem movent dum sensus externi quiescunt et memoria correctionem praesentis rei non suppeditat.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D11","text":"Cogitatio voluntaria non imagines ad nutum creat, sed ex copia iam praesenti imagines attentioni congruentes seligit.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D12","text":"Motus voluntarius procedit ab imagine motus ad voluntatem, a voluntate ad animam per membra diffusam, atque inde ad corpus aere adiutum.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A16","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D13","text":"Somnus oritur cum ictus externi et interiores dispositionem animae perturbant, partem expellunt et partem in interiora contrudunt.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A5","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A8","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D14","text":"Fames et sitis sunt effectus amissionis corporum, rarefactionis membrorum et necessitatis materiam congruentem restituendi.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A7","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D15","text":"Utilitas membrorum est effectus posterior structurae iam natae, non causa originis eius.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D16","text":"Voluptas Venerea utrique sexui communis esse potest quia utriusque corpus congruo ictu et mutuo ardore movetur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A5","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A7","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D17","text":"Amor exclusivus crescit cum simulacra, memoria et opinio idem obiectum continenter repetunt, quamvis corpus ex imaginibus satiari non possit.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A13","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D18","text":"Similitudo, varietas hereditaria et fecunditas ex proportione, mixtura et compatibilitate duplicis seminis oriuntur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A2","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A7","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A19"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:SD1","text":"Visio, auditus, odoratus, gustus, cogitatio et cupiditas unam grammaticam materialem emissionis, itineris, ictus et congruentiae variant.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A5","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A7","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A8","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:SD2","text":"Veritas sensibilis et falsitas iudicialis ad diversos gradus pertinent, unde apparentia servari potest dum interpretatio corrigitur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A12","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A13","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A14","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:SD3","text":"Apparitiones mortuorum, monstra, deos locorum et motus somniorum explicatio materialis ex indicibus alterius mundi in effectus transmissionis reclasificat.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D7","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D9","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:SD4","text":"Agens humanum non est principium motus a materia separatum, sed nexus imaginum, attentionis, voluntatis, animae et corporis.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A10","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A16","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A17","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:SD5","text":"Facultates biologicae et usus historice emergunt ex structuris, congruentiis et consuetudinibus iam constitutis.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A15","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D14","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D15","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:SD6","text":"Amor est circuitus recursivus in quo imago cupiditatem excitat, cupiditas opinionem auget, opinio attentionem figit, et attentio imaginem perpetuat.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A13","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A18","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:SD7","text":"Continuitas apparentis rei vel motus ex successione celerrima formarum pereuntium et substitutarum construitur.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A3","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A4","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A9","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D1","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:SD8","text":"Correctio affectuum fit non sensibus repudiatis, sed opinionibus retractatis, attentione conversa et imaginum pabulo interrupto.","refs":["CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A11","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:A13","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D6","CH_0T6T_LIBQ:D17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:DNX1","text":"Qualitates sensibiles non sunt valores absoluti in obiecto clausi, sed relationes inter figuras incidentes et structuram recipientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:DNX2","text":"Nulla perceptio fit per accessum incorporeum aut sine medio ad essentiam rei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:DNX3","text":"Stabilitas imaginis non requirit formam permanentem, quia successio formarum discretarum effectum continuitatis praestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:DNX4","text":"Voluntas non incipit ex nihilo, sed ab imagine praevia et dispositione materiali dependet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:DNX5","text":"Futurus usus non potest esse causa temporalis organi iam ante usum constituti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:DNX6","text":"Pulchritudo amata non continet necessario perfectiones quas cupiditas ei attribuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:DNX7","text":"Mens non stat extra naturam ut imaginum fluxum absolute regat aut sensuum testimonium ex fundamento extrinseco iudicet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:DNX8","text":"Causa divina admitti non debet ubi differentia figurarum, motuum et congruentiarum effectum sufficit producere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0082","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:SNX1","text":"Systema nullo ordinatore providentiali indiget qui sensus, membra, cupiditates aut generationem ad fines praestitutos dirigat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0082","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:SNX2","text":"Nullum tribunal cognitionis extra sensus et ab eis independens praesto est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:SNX3","text":"Nullum subiectum personale permanens dissolutionem corporis et animi integrum superat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:SNX4","text":"Possessio totalis corporis amati impossibilis est, quia amanti simulacra tantum incorporantur, non ipsum corpus alterius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:SNX5","text":"Praesentia immobilis rerum excluditur, quoniam perceptio et vita ex fluxu, ictu, substitutione et recompositione constant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:FGS1","text":"Primordia figurata → compositio rerum → effluxus corporeus → transmissio → ictus recipientis → affectio sensibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:FGS2","text":"Superficies rei → simulacrum formam retinens → motus per aerem → oculus percussus → species rei → distantia ex aere propulso.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:FGS3","text":"Affectio sensibilis vera → opinio animi addita → falsa causalitatis vel identitatis assignatio → ratio sensibus innixa → distinctio dati ab addito.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:FGS4","text":"Differentia figurarum et viarum → diversa penetratio vel repercussio → distinctio visus, vocis, odoris et saporis → varietas secundum recipientem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:FGS5","text":"Copia simulacrorum → compositio vel successio → praeparatio attentionis aut habitus → imago mentalis → cogitatio, somnium vel apparitio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:FGS6","text":"Ictus aut amissio corporum → mutatio dispositionis animae et corporis → somnus, fames, sitis vel cupiditas → restitutio aut motus compensatorius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"}]},{"id":"CH_0T6T_LIBQ:FGS7","text":"Structura nata → actio possibilis → repetitio → usus agnitus → ars vel consuetudo; futurus usus causam originis non constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_0T6T_LIBQ:PR6FEF796CE4799255:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"revised-passages"},{"id":"RAW_0T6T_